This is my old vim configuration, parts of it date back to 2004 when I first switched from pico to vim on FreeBSD 5.2.1-RELEASE. 
I fiddled and futzed with it constantly, when I became a developer in 2007, there were A LOT of changes to be made, and I created
my dotfiles/ repo including the cobbled mess of a .vimrc file with the rest of my .zshrc, .screenrc and other assorted config
files I needed at the time. The fiddling never stopped to any of these files, and eventually I broke up my vim and zsh files into
a module format

01_globals.vim  
02_colorscheme.vim  
03_keybindings.vim  
04_functions.vim  
05_buffers.vim  
06_statusline.vim

and used the .d naming scheme .vim.d/ with .vimrc becoming a forloop. Anyways, at the end of 2017 I changed jobs and no longer
write code like I used to and over the years these plugins have either stopped working, or I haven't used in years and recently
I made a lifestyle change and switched to Helix as my primary editor. While I still use vim, I no longer need 4GBs of plugins and 
keystrokes many of which I've long forgotten. So I am storing them here, for posterity's sake. 

This repo is available to do anything you want to with it, I didn't bother putting a license on it as some plugins use GPL, 
some maybe an Apache or MIT license and I don't care enough to dig through so this repo is released under the terms of the 
license on each plugin, if applicable, it's up to you to look and find out how much you care.
